 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Each log is \"transaction_id,account_id,amount,timestamp\" (amount a signed integer; the fourth field is inferred to be an integer timestamp). Output rows [account_id, balance] (integer) sorted by account_id in code-point order, one per account seen. Level 3: drop duplicate ids (first in input order wins), then apply the rest in timestamp order (ties keep input order); a log whose application would make the balance negative is rejected. Return [balances, rejected transaction ids in processing order]. Accounts that only appear in rejected logs are still listed (balance 0 or unchanged).",
  "provenance": [
